## Key Concepts

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **GOT** | Table of pointers to libc functions, writable at runtime |
| **PLT** | Stub that reads the GOT to find the real function address |
| **GOT overwrite** | Write a new address into a GOT slot to hijack any libc call |
| **`exit()` hijack** | Program calls `exit` — we make it call `o()` instead |
| **`%4$n`** | Same position as level 3 — direct `printf` call in same frame |
| **Hidden function** | `o()` exists in the binary but is never called normally |